306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 242 0 R
/E (Hereditary cancers arise from inherited genetic variants that can substantially increase an individual's susceptibility to cancer. Advances in cancer genomics have made large-scale mutation and clinical datasets available for computational risk assessment. Conventional risk assessment often relies on individual cancer types, specific genes, or predefined clinical criteria, limiting the ability to capture complex interactions across multiple risk factors. Machine Learning provides an opportunity to integrate genomic variants with clinical characteristics and identify complex patterns associated with cancer risk.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
